        "title": "ci(deadcode): restore enforced unused-export ratchet",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe unused-export baseline claimed that new entries fail CI, but the dependency shard stopped invoking `deadcode:exports` in #105704. At the same time, Knip's test-support exclusions lived under `ignoreFiles`, which only suppresses unused-file findings; unused exports and types from those files still inflated the baseline.\n\nRelated: #105575, #105595.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Move test-support patterns to Knip's top-level `ignore`, while keeping production `live-*` files under `ignoreFiles` so their exports remain analyzed.\n- Restore `deadcode:exports` in the dependency shard. Current targets must provide the script; historical targets run it when their checkout supports it and otherwise retain the legacy fallback.\n- Add guard tests for the Knip option semantics and current/historical CI behavior.\n- Refresh the baseline from 5,705 entries on the reviewed starting point to 5,570 exact entries after concurrent-main cleanup. This is configuration-driven cleanup plus a small hand-reviewed residue, not a mechanical export burn-down.\n- Preserve the shipped `packages/gateway-client` timeout export while removing its duplicate core re-export. Remove one obsolete session patch writer whose production callers had already migrated.\n- Hand-classify fresh concurrent-main residue: internalize genuinely private exports; retain exported-signature types, explicit test hooks, and protocol surfaces deliberately.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-facing behavior change. CI now enforces that unused exports cannot grow silently, while intentional test and protocol surfaces remain intact.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact-head `deadcode:exports`: 5,570-entry match in CI run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29218910871 (`check-dependencies`).\n- Exact-head touched-surface CI: dependency ratchet, guards, session-accessor boundary, production/test TypeScript, and full lint passed in run 29218910871.\n- Focused ratchet/gateway/session/plugin proof: 314 tests passed across six Vitest shards on `crimson-lobster-b31f`.\n- Focused auth/config/gateway/restart/plugin residue proof: 126 tests passed across six Vitest shards on `swift-crayfish-a34a`.\n- Final ratchet/CI-guard proof: 61 tests passed on Blacksmith Testbox `pearl-crab-acf3` (`tbx_01kxckhg8v7tv4hrry7qa9m0nv`); Actions run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29218761041.\n- `pnpm build`: passed on Blacksmith Testbox `silver-shrimp-49a9`; Actions run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29216453346.\n- Broad `pnpm check:changed`: passed in Crabbox run `run_b800202102f3`.\n- Fresh full-branch autoreview after conflict resolution: clean, no actionable findings (0.90 confidence).\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n- Known unrelated current-main noise in run 29218910871: native inventory drift and its Apple i18n test duplicate (fixed by `c029d997a98`), plus the existing plugin-SDK declaration-size ceiling.\n",
